# Hook scripts are executable content that runs automatically on every
# contributor's machine once the folder is trusted (see GHSA-ph6w-f82w-28w6).
# Every change to a guardrail, a permission rule, the installer, the tools, the
# tests or the CI workflows is routed to the owners below for security review.
# With a single maintainer that review is advisory, not enforced: GitHub does not
# let an author approve their own pull request, so branch protection on main
# requires the CI checks instead — the test suite on both OSes and the
# policy-change release gate — and not an approving review. A repository with a
# second reviewer should also require code-owner review in branch protection.
#
# Consumers who install this baseline should add the equivalent rule to their
# own repo:  /.claude/**  @their-security-team
#
# Maintainer. Replace with a security team handle if ownership moves.

/hooks/                       @topazyo
/lib/                         @topazyo
/tools/                       @topazyo
/managed/                     @topazyo
/examples/                    @topazyo
/settings.template.json       @topazyo
/baseline.config.json         @topazyo
/baseline.config.schema.json  @topazyo
/install.sh                   @topazyo
/.gitattributes               @topazyo
/tests/                       @topazyo
/.github/                     @topazyo
/SECURITY.md                  @topazyo
/RELEASING.md                 @topazyo

